  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Created at a collaborative performance called "Typeface" on July 15, 2017 at the Visual Art Exchange in Raleigh, NC. The artists stood facing each other, with typewriters on pedestals about eight feet apart. A looped scroll went through both typewriters. The artists typed simultaneously on the same paper scroll, colliding the language and responding to each other's writing in the moment. Along one wall of the gallery, a horizontal dowel was hung, on which finished scrolls were installed for visitors to handle and read -- Summarized from website of Heather Gordon (http://heathergordon.transition-project.com/typeface-performance-at-vae/).</subfield>
  </datafield>
